cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its compiled data, please cite it as below."
title: "Strike: Singapore Business Electricity Price Advisory"
abstract: >-
  Analytics for Singapore commercial and industrial electricity buyers deciding
  when to lock a fixed price, stay on the regulated tariff, or float on wholesale.
  Compiles real half-hourly USEP, system demand, ancillary reserve prices, Load
  Curtailment Price and Temporary Price Cap parameters from the Energy Market
  Company NEMS feed, together with the EMA quarterly regulated tariff and its
  component breakdown. Provides a three-way cost comparison, a fair value
  reference built from two independent published anchors, a load-shift optimiser,
  Demand Response revenue estimation, and a backtested short-term price forecast.
type: software
authors:
  - alias: "olenny-coder"
repository-code: "https://github.com/olenny-coder/sg-electricity-strike-rate"
url: "https://strike-glik.onrender.com/"
keywords:
  - Singapore
  - electricity prices
  - USEP
  - Uniform Singapore Energy Price
  - regulated tariff
  - energy procurement
  - demand response
  - energy analytics
  - price forecasting
  - open data
